      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:2:3:13:18",
      "text": [
        " سَمِعْتُ أَبَا إِبْرَاهِيمَ ( عليه السلام ) يَقُولُ مَنِ اسْتَكْفَى بِآيَةٍ مِنَ الْقُرْآنِ مِنَ الشَّرْقِ إِلَى الْغَرْبِ كُفِيَ إِذَا كَانَ بِيَقِينٍ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Al Husayn Bin Ahmad Al Minqary who said, ",
          "‘I heard Abu Ibrahim<sup>asws</sup> (7<sup>th</sup> Imam<sup>asws</sup>) saying: ‘The one who suffices with one Verse from the Quran from the east to the west, that would suffice him, when that was with conviction’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "18. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from al- Husayn ibn Ahmad al-Minqari who has said the following: “I heard abu Ibrahim (a.s.) saying, ‘If one considers one verse of the Holy Quran sufficient (for his protection) from East to West, it is enough [with certainty].”’ "
        ]
      }
